WEBVTT

00:07.568 --> 00:10.096
Give the boss here a bribe.

00:10.496 --> 00:12.416
It'll make the rest of your work easier.

00:12.624 --> 00:13.296
Yes, sir.

00:18.016 --> 00:20.208
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:20.208 --> 00:24.944
I am Seeker Guild supervisor Harold Jenkins.

00:25.392 --> 00:28.048
I look forward to doing business with you.

00:29.296 --> 00:32.016
Yes… Fine wine indeed.

00:32.336 --> 00:35.056
It seems the winery is doing well.

00:35.392 --> 00:38.416
Yes, I'm comfortable.

00:38.704 --> 00:42.064
Thanks in part to the inheritance
and servants my grandfather left me.

00:42.173 --> 00:43.744
How modest of you.

00:43.968 --> 00:49.504
You seem to have a natural talent
for leading people and managing groups.

00:49.920 --> 00:51.664
I don't do much of importance.

00:51.856 --> 00:56.144
I plan to step back
and leave the business to them soon.

00:56.768 --> 01:00.944
So… What could a guild inspector
want from me now?

01:02.304 --> 01:06.528
I've already given my testimony
about the tragedy that visited my town.

01:09.792 --> 01:12.400
This photo is from a few days ago.

01:13.072 --> 01:17.968
We suspect it's the same Lord
that manifested in your town.

01:18.992 --> 01:20.176
This thing…

01:20.688 --> 01:23.280
You don't look very surprised.

01:23.648 --> 01:27.216
No. I guessed it might still be alive.

01:28.064 --> 01:31.632
There were two things that should
have been there that day and weren't.

01:32.256 --> 01:35.520
The Lord's body, and my grandfather's battleaxe.

01:36.272 --> 01:37.632
Has it been dealt with?

01:38.048 --> 01:43.248
A major clan called Night Rage went to fight it,
but they were defeated.

01:43.616 --> 01:46.032
By the time we sent Supreme Dragon after them,

01:46.032 --> 01:49.152
the Lord had gone back to the Void.

01:49.568 --> 01:50.672
It went back?

01:51.168 --> 01:57.088
They say beasts try to conquer our world
out of uncontrollable instinct.

01:57.088 --> 02:02.723
However, this one is thought
to manifest intentionally.

02:02.944 --> 02:06.368
This is the Lord that defeated Overdeath.

02:06.368 --> 02:11.293
It is possible that its second manifestation

02:11.427 --> 02:14.894
has given it enough experience
to become a new Valiant.

02:15.424 --> 02:21.440
A Valiant… Like the Ten Dark Lords
at Abyssal Depth 13.

02:21.728 --> 02:26.864
I understand each one of them
has enough power to destroy our entire world.

02:27.280 --> 02:32.176
The last known time a Valiant appeared
was forty years ago.

02:32.464 --> 02:38.144
Cocytus the Silverfish wiped out
three nations in the blink of an eye. But…

02:38.241 --> 02:42.112
My grandfather's clan,
the Bloodsword Federation, defeated it.

02:42.512 --> 02:45.040
It was a first in human history.

02:45.429 --> 02:49.663
We'd thought we had no option
but to force Valiants back to the Void,

02:49.664 --> 02:52.078
and yet we emerged victorious against one.

02:52.464 --> 02:53.632
However…

02:54.128 --> 02:57.648
This one may cause yet another
disaster for humanity.

02:58.205 --> 02:59.671
Is that what you mean to say?

02:59.813 --> 03:01.813
Regrettably, yes.

03:04.016 --> 03:05.104
Interesting.

03:07.216 --> 03:08.384
Just like him.

03:09.552 --> 03:14.016
Your eyes look like Brandon's…
your grandfather's.

03:14.448 --> 03:18.304
I was the inspector assigned
to the Bloodsword Federation.

03:18.304 --> 03:20.940
I knew your grandfather well.

03:21.085 --> 03:25.168
So I stopped by to see
how the grandson he left is doing.

03:25.280 --> 03:28.016
I see I had no need for concern.

03:28.752 --> 03:31.456
You'll be fifteen next year.

03:31.728 --> 03:34.784
Old enough to be recognized as a Seeker.

03:37.264 --> 03:38.976
Excuse me.

03:42.320 --> 03:43.568
Remember me.

03:45.184 --> 03:47.072
We'll meet again some day.

03:47.360 --> 03:50.832
This is the face of the man
who'll be the most powerful Seeker.

05:31.376 --> 05:34.688
So… You're sure it'll be okay?

05:34.688 --> 05:38.832
Yeah. No tricky questions. Just answer normally.

05:38.960 --> 05:47.069
But if my answers rub the inspector the wrong way,
will our clan get rejected?

05:47.136 --> 05:47.648
Nope!

05:47.780 --> 05:53.552
What? I heard that if you get on the inspector's
bad side, he can reject you on the spot.

05:53.552 --> 05:55.920
Oh no! What do I do?!

05:55.920 --> 05:58.061
If I mess this up, then Noel's dream…!

05:58.128 --> 06:00.240
You'll just have to atone by death.

06:00.304 --> 06:02.672
We didn't have long, but thanks for the memories.

06:02.672 --> 06:04.983
Just leave the rest to me and die now.

06:05.100 --> 06:07.344
You two…

06:11.152 --> 06:14.128
Oh? What's wrong, all of you?

06:14.864 --> 06:17.360
You don't have to be so nervous.

06:18.064 --> 06:20.368
Good to see you again, Noel.

06:26.656 --> 06:33.152
I see you have both a clan house
and the twenty million fil insurance fee ready.

06:33.152 --> 06:38.128
You may be inexperienced,
but you aren't lacking in knowhow, I see.

06:38.288 --> 06:43.200
I plan to rank up to B as soon as
our clan is approved.

06:43.200 --> 06:45.248
I can also move up to B.

06:45.680 --> 06:47.968
Koga will be the only C-Rank.

06:49.344 --> 06:50.960
Very well.

06:50.960 --> 06:56.080
I notice that the clan name
on your application isn't Blue Beyond.

06:56.080 --> 06:59.888
I plan to change it to that name
upon becoming a clan.

07:00.064 --> 07:01.728
I see.

07:01.744 --> 07:03.864
Well, that concludes the interview.

07:04.013 --> 07:06.368
Huh? It's over already?

07:06.448 --> 07:07.280
Yes.

07:07.520 --> 07:10.480
Your clan application is rejected.

07:13.648 --> 07:15.776
I can't believe it…

07:16.320 --> 07:20.496
He can kill an Abyssal Depth 12 Lord
all by himself?

07:20.912 --> 07:24.352
That's normal for him, though.

07:25.024 --> 07:31.536
The vice-master of one-star Regalia clan,
Supreme Dragon, known as the very strongest…

07:31.968 --> 07:35.600
Zeke Feinstein the Innocent Blade!

07:37.904 --> 07:39.712
I'll be frank with you.

07:39.712 --> 07:43.120
We're looking for stronger Seekers at the moment.

07:43.376 --> 07:47.488
Fulfilling the conditions
to form a clan isn't enough.

07:47.664 --> 07:49.872
Things have changed.

07:49.872 --> 07:51.472
What?! Why…

07:51.696 --> 07:52.848
How have things changed?

07:53.850 --> 07:56.856
Keep this between us, please.

07:57.440 --> 08:02.096
We've discovered a massive mana presence
to the west of the border.

08:02.384 --> 08:07.392
The underground mana flow is
already approaching critical speed.

08:07.392 --> 08:10.208
It's just a matter of time before it erupts.

08:10.800 --> 08:11.968
How long exactly?

08:12.425 --> 08:13.849
About a year.

08:14.320 --> 08:19.584
When the mana erupts,
a massive Abyss will immediately appear.

08:20.016 --> 08:26.176
That means a Depth-13 Lord,
a Valiant, will appear.

08:27.808 --> 08:30.272
C-Can't you stop it?

08:30.544 --> 08:35.024
The mana that flows within the earth is
like the blood flowing in our veins.

08:35.024 --> 08:38.624
Obstructing its flow can cause
earthquakes or eruptions.

08:38.624 --> 08:41.632
It would make the area unlivable.

08:42.560 --> 08:43.680
Can we kill it?

08:44.224 --> 08:48.208
We defeated Cocytus the Silverfish.

08:48.512 --> 08:51.776
That's why our empire is flourishing.

08:52.304 --> 08:54.976
The fight will have to involve a major coalition.

08:55.184 --> 08:59.488
We'll need the nation's top Seekers, the Regalia.

08:59.984 --> 09:02.160
The one-star Supreme Dragon.

09:02.160 --> 09:05.088
The two-star Kahn and Cave of the Universe.

09:05.088 --> 09:10.960
The three-star Blade Flash, Goat Dinner,
Pandemonium, and Lorelai.

09:10.960 --> 09:14.896
Each clan is worthy of their regalia.

09:15.200 --> 09:19.616
But as someone who's seen a Valiant
with my own eyes,

09:19.616 --> 09:22.336
I can't say for sure we can win.

09:22.448 --> 09:26.016
So we're looking for people
who can fight right away.

09:26.016 --> 09:30.736
We don't have the time or resources
to train rookies like you.

09:31.088 --> 09:32.176
Please understand.

09:33.184 --> 09:34.096
Okay.

09:34.400 --> 09:35.792
You're okay with that?!

09:35.792 --> 09:37.456
He has a point.

09:37.680 --> 09:40.400
We don't meet the criteria he's looking for.

09:41.136 --> 09:42.480
Not yet.

09:45.152 --> 09:45.728
Let's go.

09:45.968 --> 09:47.728
H-Hold on, Noel!

09:50.704 --> 09:52.144
My, my…

09:52.144 --> 09:56.896
Who did that sore loser remind me of again?

09:58.304 --> 10:00.240
Me, of course.

10:00.320 --> 10:01.776
My grandson makes me proud.

10:02.320 --> 10:05.152
Yes… That's right.

10:05.632 --> 10:07.248
Noel Stollen…

10:07.680 --> 10:09.440
That boy will surely…

10:12.608 --> 10:15.472
Noel! Why'd you give up on forming a clan?!

10:15.472 --> 10:16.960
Are you giving up your dream?!

10:17.936 --> 10:20.928
Giving up? Don't be stupid.

10:22.016 --> 10:26.736
This is an opportunity for us
to take a giant leap.

10:29.088 --> 10:34.144
Listen. It's true that a Valiant could
potentially wipe out the human race.

10:34.640 --> 10:37.148
But at the same time, it's a huge blessing.

10:37.824 --> 10:44.704
The defeat of Cocytus raised
the Empire's standard of living all at once.

10:45.248 --> 10:52.304
Devices built using Cocytus's heart
produced purified water for the entire nation.

10:53.120 --> 10:58.112
Defeating stronger beasts results in
advancements in magic-engineered civilization.

10:58.704 --> 11:01.808
That's exactly why Seekers are seen as heroes.

11:02.476 --> 11:07.808
Seekers are those who can turn
unprecedented disaster into divine blessings.

11:08.096 --> 11:09.328
I see…

11:10.144 --> 11:13.072
We need to get regalia as soon as possible.

11:13.808 --> 11:16.144
But we're not a clan yet.

11:16.144 --> 11:18.400
It's too early to talk about that!

11:19.968 --> 11:23.776
You said we'd have regalia
in a year's time before.

11:23.872 --> 11:24.992
Half a year.

11:26.048 --> 11:28.832
H-Half a year?!

11:29.056 --> 11:31.808
Yep. We'll have regalia in half a year.

11:32.112 --> 11:37.072
We'll gain experience to stand out
as a clan over the next few months.

11:37.808 --> 11:42.592
Ideally, we're asked to fight
against the Valiant in a year's time.

11:43.152 --> 11:50.656
If we get results then, our names will go down
in history as some of the strongest Seekers ever.

11:51.680 --> 11:53.952
An undefeated swordsman from the Far East.

11:54.368 --> 11:56.352
The granddaughter of a legendary assassin.

11:56.890 --> 11:59.546
And Overdeath's grandson.

12:00.464 --> 12:02.080
But that alone isn't enough.

12:02.400 --> 12:04.096
There's no time to dawdle.

12:04.688 --> 12:06.953
To get regalia as fast as possible,

12:06.954 --> 12:11.344
we'll have to already have skill and knowledge
when we become a clan.

12:11.344 --> 12:13.726
Extra! Extra!

12:13.840 --> 12:16.544
Another feat by Zeke of Supreme Dragon!

12:16.736 --> 12:19.792
He's defeated a Depth-12 Lord!

12:20.720 --> 12:22.832
What we need is drama.

12:23.280 --> 12:26.016
An event that grabs the public's attention.

12:26.464 --> 12:28.880
A story that grips them.

12:32.128 --> 12:33.216
Don't worry.

12:34.304 --> 12:36.464
I'll come up with the plan.

12:38.032 --> 12:41.024
[IX - A Snake Hones Its Fangs]

12:41.888 --> 12:47.728
Your desired new power
as a Talker is Strategist. Am I correct?

12:47.984 --> 12:49.408
Yes. Go ahead.

12:49.712 --> 12:53.024
Then I shall start the ceremony.

12:53.696 --> 12:56.864
I shall open a new door for thee.

12:57.296 --> 13:00.496
Thou whom desirest great power…

13:00.880 --> 13:04.128
Turn thine eyes to the sea within thee.

13:04.128 --> 13:07.888
The light of wisdom shall shine
on the water's darkness.

13:07.888 --> 13:11.376
That light shall be as a door to this world.

13:12.592 --> 13:15.376
I shall open thy door…

13:17.824 --> 13:21.520
Strategist. A B-Rank Talker-class Job.

13:21.888 --> 13:24.688
It's characterized by
highly boosted cognitive processing.

13:25.040 --> 13:31.360
I can analyze battles in real time
and instantly give orders based on my predictions.

13:33.760 --> 13:35.600
Zeke is so dreamy!

13:36.120 --> 13:38.856
Can we go out to eat? My treat.

13:39.536 --> 13:41.280
Zeke Feinstein.

13:41.632 --> 13:44.128
Oh? If I recall, you're…

13:44.352 --> 13:45.968
What do we have here?

13:46.208 --> 13:50.800
If it isn't Zeke Feinstein, vice-master of
Supreme Dragon, the strongest clan in the nation.

13:51.504 --> 13:52.976
It's an honor to meet you.

13:53.296 --> 13:58.240
My pleasure. I've heard about you, Noel Stollen.

13:58.592 --> 14:03.312
There are three Seekers
who've reached EX-Rank in the city.

14:03.312 --> 14:08.032
One is Leo Edin the King Slayer,
master of Pandemonium.

14:08.672 --> 14:13.008
One is Victor Krauser the Beginning One,
master of Supreme Dragon.

14:13.488 --> 14:20.640
And the last is the Innocent Blade,
Zeke Feinstein.

14:20.864 --> 14:25.184
You're the legendary
Seeker Overdeath's grandson, right?

14:25.392 --> 14:28.912
Yes, although I'm not much like him.

14:29.088 --> 14:35.184
You think so? Didn't you overthrow
the Gambino family?

14:35.184 --> 14:37.280
Of course not! You have the wrong man.

14:37.472 --> 14:40.304
Are you saying it's a coincidence that they got

14:40.305 --> 14:43.808
a new boss right after
those rumors started flying?

14:44.608 --> 14:48.240
I'm curious what tricks you used.

14:49.856 --> 14:50.960
I'm surprised.

14:51.488 --> 14:52.048
Hmm?

14:52.560 --> 14:57.726
That the vice-master of the
great Supreme Dragon clan

14:57.727 --> 15:01.200
would try to recruit me
in such a roundabout way.

15:01.360 --> 15:05.168
You caught me, huh?
I'll just come out with it, then.

15:05.920 --> 15:07.584
Join Supreme Dragon.

15:07.968 --> 15:09.680
- It won't be a bad deal for you…

15:09.680 --> 15:10.768
- No.
- It won't be a bad deal for you…

15:11.632 --> 15:14.576
I'm not going to work under someone else.

15:15.712 --> 15:18.016
Heh… Okay.

15:18.016 --> 15:22.896
But I'm the type of guy who'll do
whatever I have to do to get what I want.

15:23.632 --> 15:25.136
Even using force?

15:25.281 --> 15:26.992
If you want that.

15:27.152 --> 15:29.648
Then show me that force of yours.

15:31.280 --> 15:33.584
If I'm going to obey someone else's orders,

15:34.096 --> 15:36.912
I have to recognize them as the strongest first.

15:37.488 --> 15:40.528
There are three EX-Rank Seekers in the capital.

15:40.976 --> 15:43.856
Victor is getting older, so that leaves two.

15:44.304 --> 15:45.856
You and Leo.

15:46.208 --> 15:48.144
Who's stronger?

15:49.600 --> 15:50.800
You mean…

15:50.800 --> 15:54.976
You want me to prove I'm stronger than Leo?

15:55.184 --> 15:57.168
If you want to lead me,

15:57.600 --> 16:00.976
then prove to me that you're the strongest.

16:01.062 --> 16:02.192
You…!

16:02.672 --> 16:06.160
If Leo and I have an all-out fight,
one of us will die.

16:06.588 --> 16:09.085
You know we can't do that!

16:10.880 --> 16:12.080
I see.

16:12.688 --> 16:15.168
You're an incorrigible man.

16:15.408 --> 16:17.408
Thanks for the compliment.

16:17.616 --> 16:20.272
Come see me once you've done that.

16:21.520 --> 16:25.760
Hey, look. It's the second-strongest
Seeker in the city, Zeke.

16:25.767 --> 16:26.335
Ooh!

16:27.584 --> 16:31.072
He just beat a Depth-12 Lord on his own…

16:31.072 --> 16:33.184
Are you the one who said that?

16:33.488 --> 16:35.536
Yeah… It was me…

16:36.032 --> 16:40.064
You said second-strongest. Why was that?

16:40.256 --> 16:41.824
Well, Leo is…

16:41.824 --> 16:47.520
I haven't fought Leo yet. How do you know
I'm not as strong as him?

16:47.952 --> 16:53.104
Well, Leo's defeated more Lords
on his own, so everyone says…

16:57.632 --> 16:58.736
Second best…

16:59.584 --> 17:02.768
I see. That's his weak spot.

17:03.248 --> 17:07.456
I'd better hurry up and form a clan
before he gets to be trouble.

17:13.424 --> 17:15.008
Quick Attack!

17:15.360 --> 17:16.336
Where…?!

17:20.432 --> 17:22.832
All right! I win again!

17:27.680 --> 17:30.512
You're not very good at backlining, Alma.

17:30.512 --> 17:32.784
My attacks are too simple?

17:32.784 --> 17:35.552
You get too heated.

17:35.552 --> 17:38.640
You didn't notice I was in range earlier.

17:39.808 --> 17:43.616
A backliner's job is to keep the battlefield
in control by keeping tabs on the fight.

17:43.792 --> 17:46.944
You need to keep your cool
and pay attention to the big picture.

17:46.944 --> 17:48.672
Noel is a good example.

17:49.088 --> 17:51.792
Maybe I should be an Assassin after all.

17:51.792 --> 17:53.264
I think so too.

17:53.536 --> 17:58.144
Party balance is important,
but I'm sure Noel will make good use of you!

17:58.848 --> 18:01.536
Hey! Lycia!

18:01.536 --> 18:02.831
Ophelia!

18:03.046 --> 18:04.352
It's been forever!

18:04.352 --> 18:07.072
Imagine seeing you here.

18:07.072 --> 18:08.096
Combat training?

18:08.257 --> 18:11.132
Yep. Are you on your way back?

18:11.232 --> 18:12.528
Yeah, we are!

18:12.601 --> 18:15.376
Who's she? A new party member?

18:15.376 --> 18:16.576
No, I'm…

18:16.576 --> 18:19.468
This is my friend! My BFF!

18:19.568 --> 18:24.976
Her name's Alma. She just became a Seeker,
so I'm showing her the ropes!

18:24.976 --> 18:27.536
Ooh, so you're her mentor!

18:27.952 --> 18:30.864
This is Ophelia from the Winged Knights.

18:30.864 --> 18:34.288
She's from the same village as me,
and she's an Archer too.

18:34.429 --> 18:35.456
Nice to meet you.

18:36.218 --> 18:37.274
You too.

18:37.936 --> 18:39.601
We have four members.

18:41.024 --> 18:43.904
This scary-looking Lancer is Keim.

18:44.046 --> 18:45.904
Who're you calling scary-looking?

18:46.576 --> 18:49.504
This furry fellow is our Summoner, Vaclav.

18:49.728 --> 18:50.640
Hi.

18:50.960 --> 18:54.288
And this is our dependable leader…

18:54.288 --> 18:55.984
Leon Fredric.

18:56.656 --> 19:01.952
They're the dependable ones.
I'm just here to look pretty as leader.

19:02.256 --> 19:05.344
You can come to us if you ever need help!

19:05.445 --> 19:07.696
I'd be happy to help Lycia's BFF!

19:07.696 --> 19:08.672
Rooting for you!

19:09.200 --> 19:10.784
You're nice.

19:10.784 --> 19:13.328
Seekers gotta help each other out.

19:13.328 --> 19:16.912
Especially with the weirdos
throwing their weight around lately.

19:16.912 --> 19:18.336
- Oh, that's not…

19:18.336 --> 19:19.408
- Noel Stollen.
- Oh, that's not…

19:19.488 --> 19:21.712
You should watch out for that guy.

19:21.712 --> 19:24.640
He's leader of a party called Blue Beyond.

19:24.976 --> 19:28.512
He's sold his party members as slaves
and done deals with the mob.

19:28.512 --> 19:31.360
There's nothing but bad news about him.

19:31.936 --> 19:33.536
That's mean.

19:33.536 --> 19:34.640
I know, right?

19:34.736 --> 19:39.088
- I heard he got some new members,
but I'm sure they're up to no good just like him.

19:39.088 --> 19:39.440
- Ophelia.
- I heard he got some new members,
but I'm sure they're up to no good just like him.

19:39.440 --> 19:40.010
- Ophelia.

19:41.056 --> 19:43.632
You shouldn't judge people just by gossip.

19:43.936 --> 19:48.080
And don't tell rookies things
you don't know are true for sure.

19:48.224 --> 19:49.248
But…

19:49.248 --> 19:52.576
I hate when people gossip
about someone they've never met.

19:53.136 --> 19:53.952
Sorry.

19:54.272 --> 19:56.240
Let's get going, Leon.

19:56.528 --> 19:59.216
Let's get some grub at the Rock-Hard Beak!

20:00.016 --> 20:01.008
Well, see you.

20:03.776 --> 20:05.152
Sorry, Alma!

20:05.152 --> 20:07.152
She's a nice person, but…

20:07.384 --> 20:09.593
It's okay. It was mostly true.

20:14.128 --> 20:17.856
So, boss, what are you plotting this time?

20:18.096 --> 20:24.704
You don't need a list of parties
who've reached B Rank unless you're up to no good.

20:25.376 --> 20:30.448
This one's a cut above the rest
in both skill and knowhow.

20:31.888 --> 20:34.528
I can't believe they're not a clan yet.

20:34.528 --> 20:37.216
I hear they're a humble and trustworthy party.

20:37.632 --> 20:43.232
In an industry with troublemakers,
good conduct must make you stand out.

20:43.440 --> 20:47.616
People might not admit it,
but everyone loves a hero of justice.

20:48.544 --> 20:51.808
He's like a knight in shining armor, right?

20:52.048 --> 20:54.720
He's not just handsome, he's skilled.

20:55.328 --> 20:57.744
He's gotta be the top B-Rank Seeker.

20:58.144 --> 20:59.648
Top, huh…

21:00.288 --> 21:03.792
Oh, right. You're B-Rank now.

21:03.952 --> 21:05.680
Awesome. Congrats.

21:05.984 --> 21:07.904
Enough of the empty praise.

21:08.640 --> 21:10.304
All right. I've decided.

21:10.304 --> 21:12.064
Cheers!

21:12.368 --> 21:15.408
Leon! We got so much done on this trip!

21:15.408 --> 21:17.632
Great job on that attack.

21:17.856 --> 21:20.128
It was all thanks to you guys.

21:20.560 --> 21:23.808
I couldn't have done it on my own.

21:23.808 --> 21:25.744
Thanks for backing me up, Keim.

21:26.144 --> 21:28.752
No, it was thanks to you, Leon.

21:28.800 --> 21:32.304
Yeah! When we went out before…

21:32.912 --> 21:35.616
Everyone has a weakness.

21:36.304 --> 21:41.664
Not even the strongest man in the city,
Zeke Feinstein, is an exception.

21:42.176 --> 21:46.112
When you strike their weak point,
their smile fades and their cracks begin to show.

21:47.024 --> 21:48.208
Boss…

21:48.576 --> 21:50.880
You're looking pretty nasty.

21:51.031 --> 21:55.184
I'm not like a certain goody-two-shoes.

21:55.808 --> 21:57.456
I don't care what I have to do.

21:57.984 --> 22:02.432
I'm climbing my way to the peak.

23:35.000 --> 23:40.031
[X - The Haves and the Have-Nots]
